================================================================================
SCOPE: WHAT THE MIT LICENSE ABOVE DOES AND DOES NOT COVER
================================================================================

The MIT license above covers the source code in this repository: everything
under src/, app/, scripts/, tests/, deploy/, and notebooks/.

It does NOT cover the data this project trains on, nor the artifacts derived
from that data. Those carry the upstream dataset's terms, which are more
restrictive.

HAM10000 (training data, not committed here)
--------------------------------------------
The ISIC 2018 distribution identifies HAM10000 as Creative Commons
Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 International (CC BY-NC 4.0):
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/

    HAM10000 Dataset (c) by ViDIR Group, Department of Dermatology,
    Medical University of Vienna.
    Tschandl, P., Rosendahl, C. & Kittler, H. The HAM10000 dataset, a large
    collection of multi-source dermatoscopic images of common pigmented skin
    lesions. Scientific Data 5, 180161 (2018).
    https://doi.org/10.1038/sdata.2018.161

Derived artifacts are non-commercial
------------------------------------
Trained classifier and DDPM weights, generated synthetic images, and the
published gallery are all derived from HAM10000. They inherit the
NonCommercial restriction, and any redistribution must retain attribution, a
link to the license, and an indication that changes were made. Use of this
repository's code to train on other data is not restricted by that term.

PanDerm backbone weights
------------------------
Not redistributed here. The fine-tuning path downloads the official upstream
checkpoint at run time; its own terms apply and should be checked upstream
before use.

Not for clinical use
--------------------
This is an educational and portfolio project. Nothing here is a medical
device, and no output is medical advice or fit for diagnosis or treatment.
